# What's new, for every release

- Every release (a new `fm1ception/installer/label.txt`) gets an entry in the version history,
  `web/site/fm1ception/history.html` in the FM1ShrubOS repository (live at `https://shrub.audio/fm1ception/history`).
  Newest first; older entries are never rewritten.
- Draft the entry from the commits since the last release (`git log` from the previous `Beta 1.0.0bN` commit):
  - a heading with the version as the page writes it (`1.0.0 beta 6`) and the date;
  - a few bullets in plain words, as a user would see the change, a bold lead-in for each;
  - internal work (build scripts, tests, the facts pipeline, signing) is left out.
- Show the user the entry's exact text and wait for approval (the user, 2026-11-19: "I should probably approve the type
  each time"). Nothing is published without it.
- With the text approved, in FM1ShrubOS:
  1. Add the entry to `history.html`; update `index.html`'s version line and both download links.
  2. Commit only those files (that repository often has unrelated work in progress).
  3. Deploy with `SHRUB_FIRMWARE=keep sh tools/deploy_editor.sh`, which publishes the site without touching
     Shrub's firmware, and check `https://shrub.audio/fm1ception/history` afterwards.
- The page names neither Shrub nor Hotwire.
